  "provider_query": "Which organization does the CVE program identify as the source of CVE records used by NVD",
  "answer": "**The MITRE Corporation (via the CVE List / CVE Program).**\n\nThe CVE Program states that the CVE List—launched and operated under MITRE—is the feed of CVE Records that NVD uses and then enriches. NVD (NIST) is a separate program and does not originate those records.\n\nRelevant sources:\n\n1. **CVE.org – Related Efforts** — CVE List (MITRE, 1999) feeds NVD (NIST, 2005); NVD builds on CVE Records. https://www.cve.org/about/relatedefforts\n\n2. **CVE.org – FAQs** — CVE and NVD are separate; the CVE List feeds NVD, which adds enhanced data. https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs\n\n3. **CVE.org – Program relationships** — NVD (NIST) is an external consumer; the CVE List feeds it. https://www.cve.org/ProgramOrganization/ProgramRelationshipwithPartners\n\n4. **CVE.org – FAQs (ownership)** — MITRE owns the CVE trademark; HSSEDI (MITRE FFRDC, funded by CISA) runs the CVE Program Secretariat. https://www.cve.org/ResourcesSupport/FAQs\n\n5. **NVD – General FAQs** — CVE Program is maintained by MITRE (sponsored by DHS/CISA); NVD syncs with and augments the CVE List. https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/General-FAQs\n\n6. **NVD – CVE process** — CVE program maintained by MITRE; published CVE List entries appear in NVD (typically within about an hour) and are then enriched. https://nvd.nist.gov/general/cve-process\n\n7. **NVD – CVE FAQs** — After publication to the official CVE List, NVD enriches records (references, CVSS, CWE, CPE). https://nvd.nist.gov/general/FAQ-Sections/CVE-FAQs\n\n8. **CVE.org – Structure** — Secretariat is The MITRE Corporation; MITRE is a Top-Level Root alongside CISA. https://www.cve.org/programorganization/Structure",
